\f0\fs24 \cf0 Standards for Discourse Mapping - nano pub focus\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A shared research system built around nanopublications\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 Nanopublications can provide the published claims and evidence for a larger research network. A central system could add a 
\f1\b coordination
\f2\b0  layer: helping independent teams discover relevant work, connect ideas, record interpretations, and track parallel investigations without treating everyone\'92s conclusions as a single agreed account.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Preserve the distinction between published claims and researchers\'92 interpretations. Store references to original nanopublications, while keeping each team\'92s tags, comments, and proposed connections as separate records. The W3C Web Annotation Data Model supports annotations that point to a resource without changing it. A team could therefore mark a nanopublication as \'93relevant to our replication study\'94 without suggesting that its original author made that connection.[{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.w3.org/TR/annotation-model/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 w3}}]\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Organize themes with ISO 25964 and SKOS. ISO 25964, 
\f3\i Thesauri and interoperability with other vocabularies
\f2\i0 , provides guidance for building subject vocabularies and connecting different classification systems. W3C SKOS, the 
\f3\i Simple Knowledge Organization System
\f2\i0 , makes those concepts and connections shareable on the Web. Teams can retain their own terminology while mapping related, broader, narrower, or equivalent concepts across projects.[{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.niso.org/schemas/iso25964"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 niso}}][{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 w3}}]\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Treat contextual maps as viewpoints, not universal truth. ISO/IEC 13250, 
\f3\i Topic Maps
\f2\i0 , offers a useful model for connecting subjects, relevant resources, and associations within particular contexts. A nanopublication might be important to one investigation but peripheral to another. Topic Maps is an alternative modeling framework\'97not an extra requirement for an RDF-based system\'97but its emphasis on context is valuable when designing project-specific research views.[{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.iso.org/standard/38068.html"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 iso}}][{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cdn.standards.iteh.ai/samples/40017/1a7e7d8cfb1c464480fb29a5806ec296/ISO-IEC-13250-2-2006.pdf"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 cdn.standards.iteh}}]\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Record who made each connection and how. Use W3C PROV, the provenance framework, through its Web Ontology Language representation, PROV-O. It can describe the people, software, activities, and sources responsible for an annotation or conclusion. The central system should distinguish a researcher\'92s judgment from an automated suggestion and preserve the history when either changes. PROV records origins and responsibility; it does not certify correctness.[{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-overview/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 w3}}][{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.w3.org/TR/2012/WD-prov-o-20120724/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 w3}}]\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Use RDF as the common connection layer; add OWL selectively. RDF, the 
\f3\i Resource Description Framework
\f2\i0 , lets publications, concepts, annotations, people, and projects share identifiers and relationships. OWL, the 
\f3\i Web Ontology Language
\f2\i0 , adds formal definitions that support inference. SKOS, PROV-O, and Web Annotation already fit this ecosystem, so they can work together without requiring a complex custom ontology for every project.[{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.w3.org/TR/2012/WD-prov-o-20120724/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 w3}}][{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.w3.org/TR/2005/WD-swbp-skos-core-guide-20051102/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 w3}}][{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://w3c.github.io/web-annotation/vocab/wd/index-respec.html"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 w3c.github}}]\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Make the central system an index and audit trail, not the sole owner of knowledge. As an implementation design, track each publication\'92s identifier; each annotation\'92s author, target, and timestamp; its project context; and its revision history. Give concurrent contributions separate identities rather than letting one team overwrite another. Use Web Annotation for the interpretation records and PROV for their origins, while managing permissions, private workspaces, synchronization, and conflict handling as application features.[{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.w3.org/TR/annotation-model/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 w3}}][{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-o/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 w3}}]\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Keep discovery separate from endorsement. Search tools may group publications by shared themes or suggest connections, but a search match should not become an accepted research claim automatically. Preserve the difference between \'93these concepts have related meanings,\'94 represented with SKOS, and \'93this team found these publications useful together,\'94 recorded as an attributed annotation. That distinction allows a shared system to support disagreement and exploration without manufacturing consensus.[{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.w3.org/TR/annotation-model/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 w3}}][{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.w3.org/TR/skos-reference/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 w3}}]\
}